Nora (docs): Quick ask — the error-ref still says 'trim context on 429' but no concrete recipe for cases where the server returned partial tokens. Can we add a super-compact pattern (detect 429, honor Retry-After if >=1s, drop oldest non-system turns until under token target, retry with capped backoff + jitter) and a tiny JS snippet? Keep it skimmable.

Jae (sdk): Yep. Ill produce a 10-line JS example and a 1-line migration tip linking to retry-utils.trimAndRetry. Recommend message-level trimming (dont touch system messages) and logging any partial header.

Pri (eng-runtime): Runtime now sets x-partial-ok=1 and x-partial-tokens=<n> when we returned partial content. SDK surfaces err.partialTokens. Suggest callout: "If partial tokens present, reconcile before replaying side-effects."

Marta (devex): Well need two short UX lines for the docs banner: "Trying trimmed context..." and "Waiting before retry..." I can add es/fr after the copy lands.

Jae (sdk): Draft JS snippet (very short):
```js
// trim oldest non-system turns, honor Retry-After, retry up to 3 times
async function sendTrimRetry(client, convo, target=2600){
  for(let attempt=0; attempt<3; attempt++){
    try { return await client.generate({conversation:convo}); }
    catch(e){
      if(e.status!==429) throw e;
      const ra=parseFloat(e.headers?.['retry-after']||'0');
      await sleep(ra>=1?ra*1000:Math.pow(2,attempt)*300 + Math.random()*120);
      while(convo.length && tokenCount(convo)>target){ if(convo[0].role==='system') break; convo.shift(); }
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```

